FactionBackstory (
    faction_id: "ronin",
    canonical_name: "The Ronin Combine",
    motto: "Bind. Cut. Carry.",
    summary: "An itinerant mercenary clan bound by a two-century ancestral debt to House Yamamoto. Ronin doctrine prizes patience, ambush, and ritual one-on-one duels. Deep red and gold ceremonial robes over light power armor; crossed katanas and binding thread on every banner.",
    history: "The Combine was founded after the Sun Wars of 2049, when the last orbital strike on Yokohama killed twenty-eight thousand civilians and one daimyo, and House Yamamoto chose to absorb the survivors of three competing clans rather than let the Coalition pacify them. The agreement was simple: the clans would survive as a single mercenary fellowship, bound by oath to House Yamamoto for two hundred years and one day. The day expires in 2249. Nobody inside the Combine has publicly mentioned this. Nobody outside has noticed.\n\nFor seventy years the Ronin were a curiosity — a martial order with no territory, fighting for House Yamamoto's banking interests against pirate cells in the Belt. They were precise. They were quiet. They did not lose anyone they did not intend to lose. By 2120 the Combine had grown beyond House Yamamoto's payroll and into the open market, taking contracts from Coalition, Frontier, and Collegium clients simultaneously, with no apparent conflict between them. The Ronin do not betray contracts. They also do not finish them ahead of schedule. Both habits have kept the Combine alive through three Sol-system economic collapses.\n\nIn the modern era, a Ronin contract is the standard against which other mercenaries are measured. Combine cells operate as five-to-twelve-person teams; each cell is led by a master swordsman who carries an ancestral named weapon. The names are recorded; the blades are sworn. When a master falls, the blade is returned to House Yamamoto and reissued to a successor, with the new name added to the inner hilt. The most senior named blade in current service is Lasting Iron, carried by Daisuke Lasting-Iron, who has not lost a duel in nineteen years and has not refused one in twenty-three. The most junior is Three Cuts, currently carried by Akihiro of Three Cuts; he is forty-one and has been a master for eight months.",
    philosophy: "A debt is the only honest currency. Bind your target with terms; cut the enemy with intent; carry your dead home, because the dead are owed that, and the Combine pays its debts. Combat is a duty, not a sport. Ronin officers prefer to settle disputes through ritual single combat when possible — not for the spectacle, but because two-on-two is twice as likely to leave a witness who tells a different story. The Combine does not seek glory; the Combine seeks the closure of the contract.",
    relationships: [
        FactionRelation (other: "coalition", stance: "professional_respect", notes: "Coalition officers commission Ronin contracts when the political optics of a Coalition strike are unfavorable. The arrangement is officially deniable and informally common. Ronin masters refuse to take Coalition contracts against the Frontier when the Frontier holds an older Combine contract; this rule has bought the Frontier survival on at least three occasions."),
        FactionRelation (other: "frontier", stance: "transactional_respect", notes: "The Frontier hires Ronin for sieges they cannot finish. The Ronin take the contract, finish the siege, and leave the salvage to the Frontier crew. Frontier leads consider this the only honest arrangement they have with any faction."),
        FactionRelation (other: "synth", stance: "philosophical_disagreement", notes: "Synth nodes calculate that Ronin contracts can be predicted and disrupted with 71% accuracy. Ronin masters consider this insulting. The Synth nodes have stopped publicizing the figure; the Ronin have stopped responding to it."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collective", stance: "religious_curiosity", notes: "The Crystalfold sing about the Combine; the Ronin do not know why. Voice of Many has refused to explain. The arrangement is interpreted by Ronin masters as a debt of unknown origin, and they treat Crystalfold settlements with corresponding care."),
        FactionRelation (other: "husks", stance: "ritual_extermination", notes: "Husks remember faces. The Combine remembers names. When the two meet, the Ronin recite the names of those the Husks have taken before they engage. The duels are short and decisive. The Husks have learned to flee from the recitation; the Ronin have learned to recite faster."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collegium", stance: "contracted_security", notes: "Collegium expeditions to anomaly-heavy zones are routinely escorted by Ronin cells. The contract terms include the safe return of all Collegium personnel and the optional disposal of any expedition findings the Combine determines to be dishonorable. The Collegium has not objected; the Collegium has, in writing, requested this clause."),
        FactionRelation (other: "starlight", stance: "courtesy_alliance", notes: "Starlight survey ships carry one Ronin master at the request of House Yamamoto, by ancestral arrangement. The master rides as a passenger and rarely intervenes. When they do intervene, the survey is complete and the ship is moving."),
    ],
    territory: "House Yamamoto holdings on Mars (the Yamamoto Halls); a single residential block on the Moon; mobile cells across Phobos; ancestral training grounds in three Belt asteroids; one closed-doors monastery on Deimos that even the Combine's own quartermasters cannot enter without permission.",
    aesthetic: "Deep red haori over dark light-armor under-suits, with gold ceremonial embroidery on the shoulders and a crossed-katana sigil at the breast. Sashes carry the named blade and a single ancestor stone. Helmets are open-faced or omitted entirely; masks are worn in transit and removed for combat. The Combine paints its emblem on the inside of every armor plate, where only the wearer sees it.",
    voice_characteristics: "Sparse. Formal. Single-clause sentences. Ronin masters use 'we' when speaking of the Combine and 'this one' when speaking of themselves; the phrase 'I' is considered crass in formal address. Humor exists but is dry, observational, and rare. When a Ronin master speaks more than ten sentences in a row, the conversation has become important."
)
